                "senderName": "NWS Juneau AK",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 20 at 2:44AM AKDT until October 21 at 4:00AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
                "description": "An atmospheric river, currently over the Yakutat area, is expected\nto continue through today. Multiple periods of heavy rain are\nexpected for the Icy Strait corridor and northeast Gulf Coast,\nincluding the following communities: Yakutat, Elfin Cove, Pelican,\nGustavus, Juneau. Elevated gusty winds are expected alongside this\nheavier rainfall, with the strongest winds from the southwest\nexpected late this morning into this afternoon. Prolonged periods of\nmoderate to heavy rain will produce significant river rises with the\npotential for at least minor flooding in Juneau and Gustavus. Ponding\nof water in low-lying areas is also possible.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The following areas, Northeast Gulf Coast and Northern\nInner Channels. This includes the cities of Yakutat, Gustavus, And\nJuneau.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, other low-lying areas and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Rain totals for the Yakutat area between this morning and this\nevening range between 4.5-7.0 inches, with greater than 9 inches\npossible at elevations greater than 1000 ft. For Gustavus, rain\ntotals ranging between 2-4 inches, exceeding 4 inches on south to\nsouthwest facing mountains along the outer coast, and exceeding 4\ninches on south to southwest facing mountains at elevation in\nGlacier Bay and around Gustavus.\n\nFor the Juneau area, rain totals have trended slightly down,\nranging between 2 and 3 inches with totals exceeding 4 inches at\nelevations greater than 4 inches. Highest rain rates are expected\nthrough early this morning into today with rain rates as high as\n0.2 inches per hour.",
                "instruction": "Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.\n\nYou should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
